> 淨利潤)","passed":0,"detail":"真實現金流充沛，無虛報帳面獲利"},{"id":5,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"財務槓桿未惡化 (ΔLeverage ≤ 0)","passed":0,"detail":"總負債資產比率 = 78.3%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"流動比率 = 0.59"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":69.43,"default_fair_val":69.43,"premium_pct":51.9,"is_undervalued":false,"pe_trailing":20,"pe_forward":17.6,"pb_trailing":1.8,"pb_forward":1.6,"div_yield":3.38,"ps_ratio":6.6,"fcf_to_ev":2.46,"fcf_to_mcap":3.8,"liab_to_assets":78.3,"cash_to_assets":0,"current_ratio":0.59,"roe":9.1,"roa":2,"moat":{"ticker":"PNW","period":"2026Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"作為一家受監管的公用事業公司，PNW 的定價權受到嚴格的監管機構審批，無法自由定價。其品牌價值在公用事業行業內相對穩定，但並非消費者決策的關鍵差異化因素。與其他公用事業公司相比，其品牌並無顯著優勢，難以形成強大的定價壁壘。因此，在品牌和定價權方面，其護城河極為薄弱。","comment_en":"As a regulated utility, PNW's pricing power is heavily constrained by regulatory approvals, preventing free pricing. Its brand value is stable within the utility sector but is not a key differentiator for consumer choice. Compared to other utilities, its brand offers no significant advantage, making it difficult to establish a strong pricing moat. Consequently, its moat in brand and pricing power is extremely weak."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"公用事業行業的核心壁壘在於其特許經營權和嚴格的監管框架。PNW 作為一家受監管的電力公司，擁有在特定區域內提供服務的專營權，這構成了顯著的進入壁壘。雖然沒有傳統意義上的專利，但其運營執照和監管批准是其業務的基石，有效阻止了競爭對手的進入。這是一種典型的受監管的特許經營模式。","comment_en":"The core moat for utilities lies in their exclusive operating licenses and stringent regulatory frameworks. PNW, as a regulated electric company, holds franchises to provide services within specific territories, creating significant barriers to entry. While not possessing traditional patents, its operating licenses and regulatory approvals are foundational to its business, effectively preventing competitors. This represents a classic regulated franchise model."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"對於電力消費者而言，更換電力供應商的轉換成本極高。基礎設施的鋪設、合約的複雜性以及消費者對穩定供應的依賴，使得用戶幾乎不可能或不願意更換供應商。一旦用戶接入 PNW 的電網，他們就高度依賴其服務，這種固有的轉換障礙為公司提供了穩固的護城河。","comment_en":"For electricity consumers, the costs associated with switching power providers are exceptionally high. The established infrastructure, complex contracts, and consumer reliance on stable supply make it virtually impossible or undesirable for customers to change providers. Once connected to PNW's grid, customers are highly dependent on its services, and this inherent switching barrier provides a solid moat for the company."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"公用事業行業的網絡效應非常有限。PNW 的電網雖然是其核心資產，但其價值主要體現在基礎設施的連接性，而非用戶之間互動產生的網絡效應。用戶不會因為更多人使用 PNW 的電力而增加其電力使用的價值，因此，網絡效應在此幾乎不存在。","comment_en":"Network effects are very limited in the utility sector. While PNW's grid is a core asset, its value lies primarily in infrastructure connectivity rather than network effects generated from user interactions. The value of PNW's electricity to a user does not increase with more people using it, thus network effects are virtually non-existent here."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"作為一家大型公用事業公司，PNW 受益於顯著的規模經濟。其龐大的發電、輸電和配電網絡能夠攤薄固定成本，使其單位成本低於小型競爭者。此外，其規模使其在採購燃料、設備和勞動力方面具有更強的議價能力。這種規模帶來的成本優勢是公用事業行業的重要壁壘。","comment_en":"As a large utility company, PNW benefits from significant economies of scale. Its extensive generation, transmission, and distribution network allows for the amortization of fixed costs, resulting in lower per-unit costs compared to smaller competitors. Furthermore, its scale provides greater bargaining power in procuring fuel, equipment, and labor. This cost advantage derived from scale is a crucial barrier in the utility industry."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"PNW 在其服務區域內擁有獨特的地理資產和基礎設施網絡，這構成了進入壁壘。其輸配電網絡是經過多年投資和擴張建立起來的，在特定地理區域內難以複製。雖然這些資產並非絕對獨特，但在其運營區域內，其主導地位和基礎設施的廣泛覆蓋使其具有一定的地理優勢。","comment_en":"PNW possesses unique geographic assets and infrastructure networks within its service territories, which form barriers to entry. Its transmission and distribution network has been built over years of investment and expansion, making it difficult to replicate in specific geographic areas. While these assets are not absolutely unique, their dominant position and extensive coverage within its operating region provide a certain geographic advantage."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"公用事業行業的運營效率至關重要，PNW 在此方面表現尚可。其運營效率主要體現在對電網的維護、故障排除和電力調度的能力上。相較於行業平均水平，其效率可能處於中等偏上，但與頂尖的、持續創新的公用事業公司相比，可能還有提升空間。監管機構的審查也促使其保持一定的運營標準。","comment_en":"Operational efficiency is critical in the utility sector, and PNW performs adequately in this regard. Its efficiency is mainly reflected in its ability to maintain the grid, troubleshoot outages, and manage power dispatch. Compared to the industry average, its efficiency might be mid-to-high, but there could be room for improvement when compared to top-tier, continuously innovating utilities. Regulatory scrutiny also compels it to maintain certain operational standards."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"PNW 的資本配置策略受到監管的顯著影響，其投資主要集中在維護和升級現有基礎設施，以滿足監管要求和服務需求。雖然其資本配置旨在維持穩定運營和適度增長，但缺乏靈活性和高回報潛力。其較低的 ROE 和 ROA 表明資本配置的回報率有待提高，與巴菲特尋求的卓越資本配置者相比仍有差距。","comment_en":"PNW's capital allocation strategy is significantly influenced by regulation, with investments primarily focused on maintaining and upgrading existing infrastructure to meet regulatory requirements and service demands. While its allocation aims for stable operations and moderate growth, it lacks flexibility and high-return potential. Its lower ROE and ROA suggest room for improvement in capital allocation returns, falling short of what is sought from exceptional capital allocators like Buffett."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"由於電力服務的必需性和高轉換成本，PNW 擁有非常高的客戶保留率。客戶通常不會主動尋求更換電力供應商，除非有極端的服務問題或顯著的價格差異（後者受監管限制）。這種被動但穩定的客戶基礎為公司提供了可預測的收入流，構成了重要的護城河。","comment_en":"Due to the essential nature of electricity service and high switching costs, PNW enjoys a very high customer retention rate. Customers typically do not actively seek to change electricity providers unless there are extreme service issues or significant price differences (the latter being regulatorily constrained). This passive yet stable customer base provides the company with predictable revenue streams, forming a significant moat."},"m10_durability":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"公用事業行業的業務模式具有天然的持久性，PNW 作為其中一員，其業務不易受到顛覆性技術的短期衝擊。電力需求是基礎性的，儘管長期來看能源轉型可能帶來變化，但其核心的電網基礎設施和服務需求將長期存在。監管框架也為其業務的穩定性提供了保障。","comment_en":"The business model of the utility sector possesses inherent durability, and PNW, as part of it, is not easily disrupted by short-term technological shocks. Electricity demand is fundamental, and while long-term energy transitions may bring changes, its core grid infrastructure and service demand will persist. The regulatory framework also ensures the stability of its operations."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Pinnacle West Capital Corporation (PNW) 是一家典型的受監管公用事業公司，其護城河主要建立在特許經營權（M2）和極高的客戶轉換成本（M3）之上，這兩者共同構成了其穩固的「收費橋」模式。規模經濟（M5）和地理資產（M6）也提供了一定的成本和進入壁壘。然而，其定價權（M1）受到嚴格監管，品牌價值有限，網絡效應（M4）幾乎為零。運營效率（M7）和資本配置（M8）表現中等，ROE 和 ROA 顯示出提升空間。客戶保留率（M9）極高，業務具有天然的持久性（M10）。總體而言，PNW 擁有一個相對穩定但受監管限制的護城河，類似於一個受保護的基礎設施資產，其增長和盈利能力受制於監管環境。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Pinnacle West Capital Corporation (PNW) operates as a typical regulated utility, with its moat primarily built upon its exclusive operating licenses (M2) and extremely high customer switching costs (M3), forming a robust 'toll bridge' model. Economies of scale (M5) and geographic assets (M6) also provide cost and entry barriers. However, its pricing power (M1) is heavily regulated, brand value is limited, and network effects (M4) are virtually non-existent. Operational efficiency (M7) and capital allocation (M8) are moderate, with room for improvement in ROE and ROA. Customer retention (M9) is very high, and the business possesses inherent durability (M10). Overall, PNW has a relatively stable but regulation-constrained moat, akin to a protected infrastructure asset whose growth and profitability are tethered to the regulatory environment.","evidenceHash":"6f1e8974bee5a76440a0ed6606f5699a5dace696be499eaa976b8d006ffd092d","assessmentPolicy":"us-buffett-moat-v3"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":3,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"distress","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-27T16:12:46.364Z","evidenceHash":"001fa530f68b966b844a98c78324105c49baebe5deee72a17e9bada53d639a9a"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":null,"reason":"incompleteCriteria","scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-27T16:12:46.364Z","evidenceHash":"001fa530f68b966b844a98c78324105c49baebe5deee72a17e9bada53d639a9a"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/PNW.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/PNW.png","website":"https://www.pinnaclewest.com","ceo":"Theodore N. Geisler","full_time_employees":"6610","description":"Pinnacle West Capital Corporation (PNW), primarily operating through its Arizona Public Service Company (APS) subsidiary, delivers retail and wholesale electricity services predominantly within Arizona. The company manages the full scope of electricity provision, encompassing generation, transmission, and distribution, leveraging a diverse energy portfolio that includes coal, nuclear, natural gas, oil, and solar power facilities. Its robust infrastructure for power delivery features approximately 5,814 pole miles of overhead transmission lines and roughly 74 miles of subterranean transmission lines. For distribution, the company maintains about 11,258 miles of overhead lines and an estimated 22,821 miles of underground primary cabling. This network is further supported by 475 owned and managed transmission and distribution substations. PNW possesses or leases roughly 6,323 megawatts of regulated power generation capacity and supplies electricity to an estimated 1.3 million customers. Established in 1985, Pinnacle West Capital Corporation's corporate headquarters are situated in Phoenix, Arizona.","description_en":"Pinnacle West Capital Corporation (PNW), primarily operating through its Arizona Public Service Company (APS) subsidiary, delivers retail and wholesale electricity services predominantly within Arizona. The company manages the full scope of electricity provision, encompassing generation, transmission, and distribution, leveraging a diverse energy portfolio that includes coal, nuclear, natural gas, oil, and solar power facilities. Its robust infrastructure for power delivery features approximately 5,814 pole miles of overhead transmission lines and roughly 74 miles of subterranean transmission lines. For distribution, the company maintains about 11,258 miles of overhead lines and an estimated 22,821 miles of underground primary cabling. This network is further supported by 475 owned and managed transmission and distribution substations. PNW possesses or leases roughly 6,323 megawatts of regulated power generation capacity and supplies electricity to an estimated 1.3 million customers. Established in 1985, Pinnacle West Capital Corporation's corporate headquarters are situated in Phoenix, Arizona.","description_zh":"**Pinnacle West Capital Corporation (PNW) 業務營運精煉報告**\n\nPinnacle West Capital Corporation (PNW) 主要透過其子公司 Arizona Public Service Company (APS) 在亞利桑那州提供零售及批發電力服務。公司業務涵蓋發電、輸電及配電的全鏈條，營運模式為整合式公用事業。\n\n其發電組合多元，包含燃煤、核能、天然氣、石油及太陽能等設施，總計擁有或租賃約 6,323 百萬瓦 (MW) 的管制發電容量。為確保電力穩定供應，PNW 建置了龐大的輸配電基礎設施，包括約 5,814 桿哩的架空輸電線路、約 74 桿哩的地下輸電線路，以及約 11,258 桿哩的架空配電線路與約 22,821 桿哩的地下主纜線。此外，公司還營運 475 座自有及管理的輸配電變電站。\n\nPNW 的營運模式著重於提供可靠且具成本效益的電力，服務約 130 萬名客戶。公司總部位於亞利桑那州鳳凰城，成立於 1985 年。","address":"400 North Fifth Street","city":"Phoenix","state":"AZ","zip":"85072-3999","country":"US","phone":"602 250 1000","full_address":"400 North Fifth Street, Phoenix, AZ 85072-3999, US","range_52w":"86.18-111.16","year_high":111.16,"year_low":86.18,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":86.18,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-08-11","name":"Blankenship Elizabeth A","title":"officer: VP, Controller and CAO","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":980,"price":99.17,"total_val":0.1},{"date":"2026-08-11","name":"Esparza Jose Luis Jr","title":"other: SVP Public Policy APS","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":1800,"price":102.01,"total_val":0.18},{"date":"2026-05-18","name":"EICHER CAROL S","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":1665,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-05-18","name":"Butler Ronald Jr","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":1665,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-05-18","name":"de la Melena Gonzalo A Jr","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":1665,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-05-18","name":"Flanagan Susan T.","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":1665,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-05-18","name":"TREVATHAN JAMES E JR","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":1665,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-05-18","name":"Sims Paula J","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":1665,"price":99.77,"total_val":0.17},{"date":"2026-05-18","name":"SPENCE WILLIAM H","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":1665,"price":99.77,"total_val":0.17},{"date":"2026-05-18","name":"Svinicki Kristine L","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":1665,"price":0,"total_val":0}],"stock_split